  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently as it stands the VRC Animator Tracking Control behavior is run locally for each viewer of the avatar. This makes it very easy for things to get out of sync, especially when multiple layers/prefabs/etc would like control over the tracking state. Because of the lack of synchronization many popular prefabs such as for face/eye tracking have to resort to continuously looping the state with the desired tracking behavior to make sure remote clients get it. Workarounds like this make it very difficult to properly use the tracking control to its full potential.\n\nAlso for the sake of backwards compatibility there should probably be a \"Local Only\" checkbox on the behavior (like with the parameter driver) that defaults on for existing content.",
